  "details": "In a fresh VRChat Avatars projects for Unity 6, we get several warnings regarding the following:\n\n```\n\nCS0672: Member 'FaceTrackingBlendshapesSetDrawer.CanCacheInspectorGUI(SerializedProperty)' overrides obsolete member 'PropertyDrawer.CanCacheInspectorGUI(SerializedProperty)'. Add the Obsolete attribute to 'FaceTrackingBlendshapesSetDrawer.CanCacheInspectorGUI(SerializedProperty)'.\n\nCS0672: Member 'FaceTrackingParameterBehaviorDrawer.CanCacheInspectorGUI(SerializedProperty)' overrides obsolete member 'PropertyDrawer.CanCacheInspectorGUI(SerializedProperty)'. Add the Obsolete attribute to 'FaceTrackingParameterBehaviorDrawer.CanCacheInspectorGUI(SerializedProperty)'.\n\n```\n\nAs it suggests in C# Rule 672, the Obsolete attribute needs to be added to those methods. Otherwise, they should be changed.",
